(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-09-22"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-09-22","label":"2026 年 9 月 22 日","date":"2026-09-22","range":"","theme":"历史","themes":["历史"],"sources":["The Guardian"],"title":"Women also helped to fund the","titleZh":"","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":14,"vocab":33,"question":20,"qa":0,"original":5,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"9.22 精读(1).pdf","headline":{"title":"Women also helped to fund the","titleZh":"","source":"The Guardian","series":"考研那些事儿之历史系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"More than 1,000 women invested in the slave trade, challenging the conventional notion that they were passive beneficiaries and largely fought for its abolition. Researchers found women bought, sold and brokered shares in the Royal African Company (RAC), South Sea Company, and other separate ventures, and used profits from the trafficking of enslaved Africans to secure financial independence and provide for their families. By the time the RAC, which trafficked about 150,000 enslaved people, was dissolved in 1752, women made up about 10% of shareholders.","zh":"超过1,000名女性曾投资于奴隶贸易，这一事实挑战了传统观念——即女性只是奴隶贸易的被动受益者，并且大多致力于推动废除奴隶贸易。研究人员发现，女性曾买卖并居间交易皇家非洲公司（RAC）、南海公司以及其他独立贸易项目的股份；她们还利用贩运被奴役非洲人所得的利润来实现经济独立，并供养自己的家庭。到1752年皇家非洲公司解散时——该公司曾贩运约15万名被奴役者——女性约占其股东总数的"},{"index":2,"en":"The Register of British Slave Traders, revealed exclusively in the Guardian, shows women from across society played an active role in financing and sustaining the transatlantic trafficking of enslaved Africans. Investors ranged from queens and princesses to titled nobility, merchants, shopkeepers and cowherds. (r)/ an official list of names or","zh":"《英国奴隶贸易商名录》此次由《卫报》独家披露。名录显示，来自社会各阶层的女性都曾积极参与资助跨大西洋贩运被奴役非洲人，并维系这一贸易体系。投资者上至王后与公主，下至受封贵族、商人、店主，乃至牧牛人。"},{"index":3,"en":"The archives include letters in which women discuss profits from “ African stock ” , while company records show one investor, Helen Gladman, asking the RAC to transport a young African girl from Sherbrooke Island in Sierra Leone to England to serve in her household. Researchers found women were involved “ at almost every level ” of the company ’ s activities. They acted as brokers, supplied goods traded on Africa’s Atlantic coast, managed company property and used their familial and social networks to strengthen the company’s finances and political influence.","zh":"档案中收录了一些女性讨论“非洲股票”收益的信件；与此同时，公司记录显示，一名投资者海伦·格莱德曼曾要求皇家非洲公司把一名来自塞拉利昂舍布鲁克岛的非洲女孩运往英国，供她家中役使。研究人员发现，女性几乎参与了公司的各个层级。她们充当经纪人，为非洲大西洋沿岸的贸易提供商品，管理公司财产，并利用家庭和社会关系网络来增强公司的财务实力及政治影响力。"},{"index":4,"en":"the University of Lila O ’ Leary Chambers, a lecturer at Cambridge who researched women ’ s involvement for the register project, said: “ This research really shows that this was not just a flash in the pan. “Across the entirety of the Royal African Company and its various guises, there were women contributing financially and expecting a financial return from the slave trade.”","zh":"剑桥大学讲师莉拉·奥利里·钱伯斯曾为该名录项目研究女性参与奴隶贸易的情况。她说：“这项研究确实表明，这绝非昙花一现。纵观皇家非洲公司及其各种不同形式的发展历程，一直都有女性在为其提供资金，并期待从奴隶贸易中获得经济回报。”"},{"index":5,"en":"Women invested from the earliest years of enslavement, from Queen Elizabeth I’s backing in the 1560s to Lady Craven’s £1,000 loan financing a voyage to the Gambia through the Guinea Company. Some investors, unable to write their names, signed company records with a spidery “X”. / money, support or approval given","zh":"早在奴役贸易起步之初，女性就已参与投资：从16世纪60年代伊丽莎白一世女王的支持，到克雷文夫人通过几内亚公司向一趟前往冈比亚的航行提供1,000英镑贷款。还有一些投资者甚至不会书写自己的名字，只能在公司记录上用歪歪扭扭的“X”签名。"},{"index":6,"en":"The research identifies 1,100 female investors across the histories of the RAC, the South Sea Company, and other separate ventures, though the true number is likely to have been higher. Of the 457 women whose marital status could be identified, almost half were widows and just over 42% were unmarried. Of the 7% who were married, most were aristocrats.","zh":"这项研究在皇家非洲公司、南海公司以及其他独立贸易项目的历史记录中确认了1,100名女性投资者，不过实际人数很可能更高。在婚姻状况可考证的457名女性中，近一半是寡妇，略高于42%的人为未婚女性。而在已婚的7%女性中，大多数属于贵族阶层。"},{"index":7,"en":"For many, the investments were crucial to gaining economic independence. Some became active traders and traded shares for friends and family, Chambers said. “ It was not a career as they would see it, but we might think: this has become your job.”","zh":"对许多女性而言，这些投资是实现经济独立的关键。钱伯斯说，其中一些人还成为积极的交易者，替亲友买卖股份。她说：“她们不会把这看作一份职业，但我们或许可以这样理解：这已经成为了你的工作。”"},{"index":8,"en":"conventional narrative that “ white women come in at the point of abolition, see the suffering of enslaved people, identify with that oppression, and then work either to reform or ultimately abolish the slave trade and slavery itself”.","zh":"钱伯斯表示，这项研究直接挑战了一种传统叙事：即“白人女性直到废奴阶段才登上历史舞台，她们看到被奴役者遭受的苦难，对这份压迫感同身受，随后致力于推动改革或者最终废除奴隶贸易以及奴隶制度本身”。"},{"index":9,"en":"Work to overturn that misconception builds on decades of scholarship by historians from the Caribbean and west Africa, including Eric Williams, Elsa Goveia and Walter Rodney. More recent public-facing projects, such as the Legacies of British Slavery archive compiled by historians at University College London, have helped bring this history to wider audiences. The archive revealed that women were among those connected to the ownership of enslaved people who received compensation after slavery was abolished in a large portion of the empire in 1833, she said. Enslaved people received nothing.","zh":"推翻这一误解的研究，建立在加勒比地区和西非历史学家数十年来的学术成果之上，其中包括埃里克·威廉姆斯、埃尔莎·戈维亚和沃尔特·罗德尼。近年来，一些面向公众的历史项目也让这段历史进入更广泛的视野，例如由伦敦大学学院历史学家整理的《英国奴隶制遗产》档案。她说，该档案显示，1833年大英帝国大部分地区废除奴隶制后，与被奴役者所有权相关的人获得了赔偿，女性也在获赔者之列。而被奴役者什么也没有得到。"},{"index":10,"en":"For Chambers, the accumulation of more than 1,000 names was itself a “gut punch” because of the lack of similar information about enslaved African women. Olivette Otele, a distinguished professor of the legacies and memory of slavery at Soas University of London, said while the lack of comparable detail about enslaved African women remained startling, “the more we know about enslavers, the better chance we have to know about enslaved women from the archives, because sometimes through diaries you can find more","zh":"对钱伯斯而言，能够汇总出1,000多个名字本身就给人“带来沉重冲击”，因为关于被奴役非洲女性的类似资料却极其匮乏。伦敦大学亚非学院研究奴隶制遗产与记忆的杰出教授奥利维特·奥特尔表示，尽管关于被奴役非洲女性的同等详实资料依然匮乏得惊人，但“我们对奴役者了解得越多，就越有可能从档案中进一步了解被奴役女性，因为有时可以通过日记找到更多细节”。"},{"index":11,"en":"She added that archives alone could not tell the full history, and future research should look at other evidence to help recover the lives and agency of enslaved women. “ These women were the transmitters and the holders of their cultures wherever they were taken from,” she said. “Through food, music, and dancing, it’s about resistance and agency, and they transmitted that.” nsi/ the capacity of a person to act","zh":"她补充说，仅凭档案无法讲述完整的历史，未来的研究还应寻找其他证据，以帮助还原被奴役女性的生活以及她们的主体性。她说：“无论这些女性被带往何处，她们都是自身文化的传递者和守护者。通过食物、音乐和舞蹈，这体现的是抵抗与主体性，而她们也将这种文化传承了下去。”"},{"index":12,"en":"The research also found that because female investors seemingly did not vote or hold board positions, they often relied on informal efforts to influence and shape a company. Meeting minutes show women acting as witnesses, running the meeting house, delivering the goods exchanged for African lives, petitioning for wages, passing information and, most importantly, lending money and buying and selling shares.","zh":"研究还发现，由于女性投资者似乎没有投票权，也没有担任董事会职务，她们往往依靠非正式的方式来影响并塑造公司。会议记录显示，女性曾担任见证人、管理会议场所、交付那些用非洲人的生命换取的商品、为工资问题请愿、传递信息，而最重要的是，她们还会出借资金以及买卖股份。"},{"index":13,"en":"Under English law, women who were single or widowed were in control of their own property and could operate as legal persons while married women could not. “That becomes really important for the Royal African Company as it stutters between financial crises,” Chambers said. “Women provided this important well of capital.” (r)/ to speak with difficulty; to make","zh":"根据英国法律，单身或丧偶女性可以自主支配自己的财产，并能够以独立法律主体的身份开展活动；而已婚女性则不能。“这一点对于皇家非洲公司而言非常重要，因为公司在一次次金融危机之间步履蹒跚，”钱伯斯说。“女性提供了这一重要的资本来源。”"},{"index":14,"en":"In the early 18th century, the RAC secretary, John Perry, wrote to female investors urging them to exchange company debts for shares and persuade friends and relatives to do the same. Chambers said: “That is a financial project, but it is also a political one, because he knows that they might not hold official positions, but women were very influential with their family members and with the way companies were perceived.”","zh":"18世纪初，皇家非洲公司秘书约翰·佩里致信女性投资者，敦促她们将公司债务兑换为股份，并劝说亲友也这样做。钱伯斯说：“这是一项金融举措，但同时也是一种政治安排。因为他知道，她们可能没有正式的职位，但女性对家庭成员以及公司在人们心目中的形象都具有很大的影响力。”"}],"vocab":[{"term":"conventional","head":"a. dj. based on what is n ˈ venʃ ə ə traditionally done or believed conventional notions about gender roles ʊʃn/ an idea, belief or opinion about","definition":"dj. based on what is n ˈ venʃ ə ə traditionally done or believed conventional notions about gender roles ʊʃn/ an idea, belief or opinion about","gloss":"传统的，惯例的【考研大纲词汇】关于性别角色的传统观念。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲 词汇"]},{"term":"notion","head":"n. / ˈ n ə something","definition":"/ ˈ n ə something","gloss":"概念，观念，看法 He has no notion of how difficult the task is. 他完全不 知道这项任务有多难。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"abolish","head":"v. to officially end a law, system, institution etc Slavery was abolished in the British Empire in 1833. ʊk /","definition":"to officially end a law, system, institution etc Slavery was abolished in the British Empire in 1833. ʊk /","gloss":"废除，废止大英帝国于 1833 年废除了奴隶制。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"broker /ˈbr ə ə","head":"n. A broker is a person whose job is to buy and sell securities, foreign money, real estate, or goods for other people.","definition":"A broker is a person whose job is to buy and sell securities, foreign money, real estate, or goods for other people.","gloss":"经纪人; 掮客 v. If a country or government brokers an agreement, a ceasefire, or a round of talks, they try to negotiate or arrange it. 斡旋 The United Nations brokered a peace in Mogadishu at the end of March. 联合国于 3 月底在摩加迪沙促成了一 场和平谈判。 (r)/ a business project or activity,","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"venture","head":"n. / ˈ ventʃ ə especially one that involves taking risks（","definition":"/ ˈ ventʃ ə especially one that involves taking risks（","gloss":"尤指有风险的） 企业，商业，投机活动，经营项目 A disastrous business venture lost him thousands of dollars. 一个彻底失败的经营项目使他损失严重。 / the activity of buying, selling or","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"trafficking","head":"n. /ˈtræfɪkɪ ŋ illegally moving people or goods","definition":"/ˈtræfɪkɪ ŋ illegally moving people or goods","gloss":"贩运；非法买卖；非法 交易 drug trafficking 毒品贩运 arms trafficking 武器贩运 trafficking in illegal goods 非法商品交易","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"register","head":"n. / ˈ redʒɪst ə items","definition":"/ ˈ redʒɪst ə items","gloss":"登记簿，花名册 The company keeps a register of all its shareholders. 公司保存着所有股东的名册。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"exclusively","head":"a. dv. only; no one else","definition":"dv. only; no one else","gloss":"唯一地，专门地，仅","example":"This offer is available exclusively to existing customers.","exampleZh":"此优惠仅面向现有客户。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"transatlantic","head":"a. dj. / ˌ trænz t ˈ læntɪk/ crossing the ə","definition":"dj. / ˌ trænz t ˈ læntɪk/ crossing the ə","gloss":"","example":"Atlantic Ocean a transatlantic flight","exampleZh":"横渡大西洋的；横越大西洋的横越大西洋的飞行","tags":[]},{"term":"range","head":"v. to vary between two limits; to include a variety （ The children's ages range from 8 to 15.","definition":"to vary between two limits; to include a variety （ The children's ages range from 8 to 15.","gloss":"在一定范围内）变化；包括（各种）【考研大纲词汇】孩子们的年龄从","example":"8","exampleZh":"岁到 15 岁不等。","tags":["考研大 纲词汇"]},{"term":"archive","head":"n. / ˈ ɑ ː kaɪv/ a collection of historical documents or records The museum holds a vast archive of wartime photographs. ʊld/ all the people living together","definition":"/ ˈ ɑ ː kaɪv/ a collection of historical documents or records The museum holds a vast archive of wartime photographs. ʊld/ all the people living together","gloss":"档案，档案室博物馆保存着大量战时照片档案。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"household","head":"n. /ˈhaʊsh ə in a house","definition":"/ˈhaʊsh ə in a house","gloss":"家庭，一户人 Most households now own at least one computer. 如今 大多数家庭至少拥有一台电脑。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"guise","head":"n. the way something appears, often hiding the truth The company operated under various guises for decades.","definition":"the way something appears, often hiding the truth The company operated under various guises for decades.","gloss":"外观，伪装，幌子这家公司数十年间以各种幌子运营。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"backing","head":"n. /ˈbækɪ ŋ to someone or something","definition":"/ˈbækɪ ŋ to someone or something","gloss":"资助，支持 The project has the backing of the government. 该项目 得到政府的支持。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"voyage","head":"n. a long journey by sea or in space They set off on a long voyage across the Atlantic. ri/ thin and bending in many","definition":"a long journey by sea or in space They set off on a long voyage across the Atlantic. ri/ thin and bending in many","gloss":"航行，航程他们启航开始横跨大西洋的漫长航程。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"spidery","head":"a. dj. / ˈ spaɪd ə directions, like a spider’s legs","definition":"dj. / ˈ spaɪd ə directions, like a spider’s legs","gloss":"细长而扭曲的，像蜘蛛腿 般的 a spidery, barely legible handwriting 细长难辨的字迹。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"marital","head":"a. dj. relating to marriage","definition":"dj. relating to marriage","gloss":"婚姻的【考研大纲词汇】","example":"Please state your age, sex and marital status. kræt/ a member of the highest","exampleZh":"请注明年龄、性别与婚姻状况。","tags":["考研 大纲词汇"]},{"term":"aristocrat","head":"n. / ˈ ærɪst ə social class","definition":"/ ˈ ærɪst ə social class","gloss":"贵族 He was born an aristocrat and inherited vast estates. 他出身贵族，继承了大片田产。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"crucial","head":"a. dj. extremely important because it will affect the final result","definition":"dj. extremely important because it will affect the final result","gloss":"至关重要的","example":"This step is crucial to the success of the project.","exampleZh":"这一步对项目成功至关重要。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"narrative","head":"n. tɪv/ a description of events, / ˈ nær ə especially one that gives a particular understanding The media's narrative about the event was misleading.","definition":"tɪv/ a description of events, / ˈ nær ə especially one that gives a particular understanding The media's narrative about the event was misleading.","gloss":"叙事，说法，叙述媒体对该事件的叙述具有误导性。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"oppression","head":"n. the cruel and unfair use of power to control a group of people The people rose up against oppression.","definition":"the cruel and unfair use of power to control a group of people The people rose up against oppression.","gloss":"压迫，压制人民奋起反抗压迫。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"overturn","head":"v. to officially change a legal decision; to reject or overturn The court overturned the earlier verdict.","definition":"to officially change a legal decision; to reject or overturn The court overturned the earlier verdict.","gloss":"推翻，撤销；颠覆法院撤销了先前的判决。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"misconception","head":"n. a wrong idea or ə understanding of something It is a common misconception that money brings happiness.","definition":"a wrong idea or ə understanding of something It is a common misconception that money brings happiness.","gloss":"误解，错误观念认为金钱带来幸福是一个常见误解。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"compile","head":"v. /k to collect information and m ˈ paɪl/ ə arrange it in a list, book or record The data was compiled from over 2,000 surveys.","definition":"/k to collect information and m ˈ paɪl/ ə arrange it in a list, book or record The data was compiled from over 2,000 surveys.","gloss":"编纂，汇编【考研大纲词汇】这些数据汇集自 2000 多份调查。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲 词汇"]},{"term":"compensation","head":"n. / ˌ kɒmpen ˈ seɪʃn/ something, especially money, given to compensate for loss, injury or damage The victims received compensation for their injuries.","definition":"/ ˌ kɒmpen ˈ seɪʃn/ something, especially money, given to compensate for loss, injury or damage The victims received compensation for their injuries.","gloss":"补偿，赔偿受害者因受伤获得了赔偿。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"distinguished","head":"a. dj. /dɪˈstɪ ŋ and admired for achievement","definition":"dj. /dɪˈstɪ ŋ and admired for achievement","gloss":"杰出的，卓越的 a distinguished professor of history 一位杰出的历史学教 授。 / unusual and surprising; difficult","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大 纲词汇","考研大 纲词汇"]},{"term":"startling","head":"a. dj. /ˈstɑːtlɪ ŋ to believe","definition":"dj. /ˈstɑːtlɪ ŋ to believe","gloss":"令人吃惊的，惊人的 The results were startling. 结果令人吃惊。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"agency","head":"n. / ˈ eɪdʒə and make their own choices","definition":"/ ˈ eɪdʒə and make their own choices","gloss":"能动性，行动力；代理机构 The film explores women’s agency in wartime. 这部电 影探讨了女性在战时的能动性。 (r)/ a person or thing that","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"transmitter","head":"n. /trænz ˈ mɪt ə passes something on to others","definition":"/trænz ˈ mɪt ə passes something on to others","gloss":"传递者，传播者；发射机 Language is a transmitter of culture. 语言是文化的传播 者。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇","考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"minutes","head":"n. a written record of what was said at a meeting Please read the minutes of last week’s meeting.","definition":"a written record of what was said at a meeting Please read the minutes of last week’s meeting.","gloss":"会议纪要请阅读上周会议的纪要。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"petition","head":"v. to ask the government or an authority for something formally Workers petitioned the mayor for safer conditions.","definition":"to ask the government or an authority for something formally Workers petitioned the mayor for safer conditions.","gloss":"请愿，正式请求【考研大纲词汇】工人们向市长请愿，要求改善安全条件。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研 大纲词汇"]},{"term":"stutter","head":"v. / ˈ stʌt ə uneven progress","definition":"/ ˈ stʌt ə uneven progress","gloss":"口吃；磕磕绊绊地进行 The economy stuttered through the decade. 这 十 年 间 经济举步维艰。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"well","head":"n. a deep hole sunk to obtain water; a source of something a well of knowledge and experience","definition":"a deep hole sunk to obtain water; a source of something a well of knowledge and experience","gloss":"井；源泉知识与经验的源泉。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】9.22 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 1 and 2, the new research challenges the conventional view by showing that women _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"remained passive beneficiaries who generally opposed the slave trade"},{"key":"B","text":"invested mainly to claim compensation after slavery was abolished"},{"key":"C","text":"actively financed and sustained the trafficking of enslaved Africans"},{"key":"D","text":"worked chiefly as sailors transporting enslaved people across the Atlantic"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·研究结论识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-2","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：More than 1,000 women invested in the slave trade, challenging the conventional notion that they were passive beneficiaries and largely fought for its abolition.","- 原文（Para.2）：The Register of British Slave Traders... shows women from across society played an active role in financing and sustaining the transatlantic trafficking of enslaved Africans.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反向观点陷阱。这正是 research 要挑战的 conventional notion。","- 选项B（错误）：时态与细节错位陷阱。女性长期投资奴隶贸易；废除后补偿只是后文另一研究涉及的内容。","- 选项C（正确）：原文连续使用 invested、financing and sustaining，说明女性是主动参与的资金供给和维系者。","- 选项D（错误）：概念偷换陷阱。研究强调股东、经纪人和物资供给，不是女性主要担任水手跨洋运输。","【命题技巧】","- 研究结论主干提取：challenging the conventional notion 之后的内容是答案核心。","- 主动/被动语义对比：passive 与 active role 构成解题信号。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"By saying the research “was not just a flash in the pan”, Chambers means that women's involvement was _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a persistent pattern rather than a short-lived occurrence"},{"key":"B","text":"an accidental discovery that suddenly produced great wealth"},{"key":"C","text":"a secret transaction hidden from company records"},{"key":"D","text":"a moral scandal that destroyed the company's reputation"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】词义猜测题·习语语境理解","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 4","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：“This research really shows that this was not just a flash in the pan.","- 原文（Para.4）：“Across the entirety of the Royal African Company and its various guises, there were women contributing financially and expecting a financial return from the slave trade.”","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：flash in the pan 指短暂、偶然的事件；not just a flash in the pan 与 across the entirety 呼应，说明女性参与具有持续性。","- 选项B（错误）：字面化陷阱。flash 不是指突然发财的意外发现。","- 选项C（错误）：无中生有陷阱。公司档案和 register 恰恰提供了可见记录。","- 选项D（错误）：答非所问陷阱。短语讨论参与持续时间，不评价公司声誉是否被摧毁。","【命题技巧】","- 习语语境去字面化：用 across the entirety 判断 flash in the pan 的否定含义。","- 持续时间线索：persistent 与 entirety 形成同义替换。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"Paragraph 9 serves to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cast doubt on the reliability of archival research on slavery"},{"key":"B","text":"separate Chambers's new findings from earlier scholarship by Caribbean and African historians"},{"key":"C","text":"show that public archives focus only on women who owned enslaved people"},{"key":"D","text":"connect the new findings to a longer effort to correct historical memory"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】篇章结构题·学术脉络功能","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 9","【解析】","- 原文（Para.9）：Work to overturn that misconception builds on decades of scholarship by historians from the Caribbean and west Africa, including Eric Williams, Elsa Goveia and Walter Rodney.","- 原文（Para.9）：More recent public-facing projects... have helped bring this history to wider audiences.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反向功能陷阱。该段是把新研究与既有学术成果连接，并未质疑档案研究可靠性。","- 选项B（错误）：逻辑偷换陷阱。builds on 表示承接和发展，不是切割分离。","- 选项C（错误）：范围偷换陷阱。档案涉及投资、补偿等联系，不能说只关注女性奴隶主。","- 选项D（正确）：builds on decades of scholarship 和 public-facing projects 表明新研究延续了纠正历史误解、面向公众传播的学术脉络。","【命题技巧】","- 学术段落功能识别：builds on 是承上启下和学术定位信号。","- 误解-修正主线：overturn misconception 概括该段在新研究中的作用。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 12-14 that women influenced company affairs mainly by _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"voting at board meetings and appointing company directors"},{"key":"B","text":"using informal networks, transactions and family influence"},{"key":"C","text":"operating as legal persons regardless of their marital status"},{"key":"D","text":"refusing to exchange company debts for shares"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·机制综合推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 12-14","【解析】","- 原文（Para.12）：The research also found that because female investors seemingly did not vote or hold board positions, they often relied on informal efforts to influence and shape a company.","- 原文（Para.13）：Under English law, women who were single or widowed were in control of their own property and could operate as legal persons while married women could not.","- 原文（Para.14）：...he knows that they might not hold official positions, but women were very influential with their family members and with the way companies were perceived.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反向事实陷阱。原文明确说她们 seemingly did not vote or hold board positions。","- 选项B（正确）：informal efforts、familial and social networks、witnesses、information、lending money 和 persuade friends and relatives 共同说明影响力来自非正式渠道。","- 选项C（错误）：限定条件偷换陷阱。法律人格属于单身或寡居女性，已婚女性不能，不能说 regardless of marital status。","- 选项D（错误）：反向细节陷阱。Perry 写信敦促女性把债务换成股份并劝说亲友，不是说她们拒绝。","【命题技巧】","- 让步-机制推理：did not vote or hold board positions 之后由 often relied on 引出真正机制。","- 跨句信息整合：法律地位、会议活动和家庭影响共同支持 informal influence。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Abolitionists First: White Women and the End of British Slavery"},{"key":"B","text":"Forgotten Investors: Women and the Financing of the Slave Trade"},{"key":"C","text":"Silent Archives: The Complete Story of Enslaved African Women"},{"key":"D","text":"Corporate Managers: How Women Governed the Royal African Company"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：Researchers found women bought, sold and brokered shares in the Royal African Company (RAC), South Sea Company, and other separate ventures, and used profits from the trafficking of enslaved Africans to secure financial independence and provide for their families.","- 原文（Para.2）：The Register of British Slave Traders... shows women from across society played an active role in financing and sustaining the transatlantic trafficking of enslaved Africans.","- 原文（Para.10）：For Chambers, the accumulation of more than 1,000 names was itself a “gut punch” because of the lack of similar information about enslaved African women.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反向主旨陷阱。文章要推翻白人女性主要站在废奴一边的传统叙述。","- 选项B（正确）：Forgotten Investors 概括超过千名女性被档案重新发现，financing of the slave trade 覆盖入股、借贷、经纪、供给和影响力等主线。","- 选项C（错误）：范围偏移陷阱。末段提到 enslaved African women 资料不足及未来研究，但不是全文完整故事。","- 选项D（错误）：程度过度陷阱。女性多无正式职位和投票权，说 governed the company 夸大其正式管理权。","【命题技巧】","- 全文对象校准：标题必须同时包含女性和奴隶贸易融资两个核心词。","- 细节与主旨区分：补偿档案、被奴役女性资料不足均为支线，不能替代主线。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.22检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["More than 1,000 women invested in the slave trade, challenging the conventional notion that they were passive beneficiaries and largely fought for its abolition. Researchers found women bought, sold and ____【11】____ shares in the Royal African Company (RAC), South Sea Company, and other separate ventures, and used ____【12】____ from the trafficking of enslaved Africans to ____【13】____ financial independence and provide for their families. By the time the RAC, which trafficked about 150,000 enslaved people, was ____【14】____ in 1752, women made up about 10% of shareholders.","The Register of British Slave Traders, revealed exclusively in the Guardian, shows women from across society played an ____【15】____ role in financing and ____【16】____ the transatlantic trafficking of enslaved Africans. Investors ranged from queens and princesses to titled nobility, merchants, shopkeepers and cowherds.","The archives include letters in which women discuss profits from “African stock”, while company records show one investor, Helen Gladman, asking the RAC to ____【17】____ a young African girl from Sherbrooke Island in Sierra Leone to England to serve in her household. Researchers found women were involved “at almost every ____【18】____” of the company’s activities. They acted as brokers, supplied goods traded on Africa’s Atlantic coast, managed company property and used their familial and social ____【19】____ to strengthen the company’s finances and political ____【20】____."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ignored"},{"key":"B","text":"brokered"},{"key":"C","text":"cancelled"},{"key":"D","text":"valued"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (brokered)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·交易行为","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] ignored（忽视）：与买卖股份的积极参与矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] brokered（撮合、经纪）：bought, sold and brokered shares 指买卖并撮合股份交易。正确答案。","[C] cancelled（取消）：不是取消股份。语义场干扰。","[D] valued（估值）：未涉及估值行为。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lessons"},{"key":"B","text":"rewards"},{"key":"C","text":"labour"},{"key":"D","text":"profits"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (profits)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·资金来源","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] lessons（教训）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","[B] rewards（报酬）：语义接近，但不如 profits 精确对应投资回报。近义干扰。","[C] labour（劳动）：女性投资者使用的是投资收益。语义场干扰。","[D] profits（利润）：used profits from the trafficking... 指利用贩运利润。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reduce"},{"key":"B","text":"describe"},{"key":"C","text":"secure"},{"key":"D","text":"postpone"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (secure)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·目标语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] reduce（减少）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] describe（描述）：不是描述独立。语义场干扰。","[C] secure（获得、稳固取得）：secure financial independence 指获得经济独立。正确答案。","[D] postpone（推迟）：与获益目标不符。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dissolved"},{"key":"B","text":"founded"},{"key":"C","text":"expanded"},{"key":"D","text":"privatised"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (dissolved)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·公司命运","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] dissolved（解散）：was dissolved in 1752 指公司于1752年解散。正确答案。","[B] founded（创立）：时间关系不合。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] expanded（扩张）：与解散相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] privatised（私有化）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"passive"},{"key":"B","text":"active"},{"key":"C","text":"minor"},{"key":"D","text":"unwilling"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (active)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·参与程度","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] passive（被动的）：与 conventional notion 中被质疑的形象相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] active（积极的）：played an active role 指发挥积极作用。正确答案。","[C] minor（次要的）：与 across society 和 almost every level 矛盾。程度差异干扰。","[D] unwilling（不情愿的）：与积极参与矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sustaining"},{"key":"B","text":"opposing"},{"key":"C","text":"recording"},{"key":"D","text":"exposing"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (sustaining)","analysis":["【题型】动名词辨析·延续语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] sustaining（维持）：financing and sustaining the trafficking 指资助并维系贩运体系。正确答案。","[B] opposing（反对）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] recording（记录）：不是仅作记录。语义场干扰。","[D] exposing（揭露）：与参与者的身份不合。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"return"},{"key":"B","text":"sell"},{"key":"C","text":"release"},{"key":"D","text":"transport"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (transport)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·位移动作","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] return（送回）：目的地是 England，不是返回原地。方向干扰。","[B] sell（出售）：后文明确是带到英国家中服役。语义场干扰。","[C] release（释放）：与服役目的相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] transport（运送）：transport a young African girl... to England 指将其运往英国。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cost"},{"key":"B","text":"level"},{"key":"C","text":"risk"},{"key":"D","text":"stage"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (level)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·抽象层级","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第2句","【解析】","[A] cost（成本）：不是成本问题。语义场干扰。","[B] level（层级、层面）：at almost every level of activities 指几乎参与各个层面。正确答案。","[C] risk（风险）：未强调风险。语义场干扰。","[D] stage（阶段）：语义接近，但 level 强调组织活动层级。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"networks"},{"key":"B","text":"duties"},{"key":"C","text":"savings"},{"key":"D","text":"degrees"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (networks)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·社会资源","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] networks（网络）：familial and social networks 指家庭与社会关系网。正确答案。","[B] duties（职责）：不是职责网络。语义场干扰。","[C] savings（储蓄）：后文还包括影响力资源。语义场干扰。","[D] degrees（程度）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"programmes"},{"key":"B","text":"campaigns"},{"key":"C","text":"influence"},{"key":"D","text":"ambitions"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (influence)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·影响力语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] programmes（项目）：不是公司项目。语义场干扰。","[B] campaigns（运动）：不是政治运动。语义场干扰。","[C] influence（影响力）：political influence 指政治影响力。正确答案。","[D] ambitions（雄心）：与 strengthen 后的宾语搭配不如 influence 精确。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.22检验题__新题型__段落排序(1).docx","type":"ordering","instructions":["Directions:"],"passage":["Part B","The following paragraphs are given in a wrong order. For Questions 41-45, you are required to reorganize these paragraphs into a coherent text by choosing from the list A-H and filling them into the numbered boxes. Paragraphs E, B and H have been correctly placed. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","[A] The Register of British Slave Traders, revealed exclusively in the Guardian, shows women from across society played an active role in financing and sustaining the transatlantic trafficking of enslaved Africans. Investors ranged from queens and princesses to titled nobility, merchants, shopkeepers and cowherds.","[B] Lila O’Leary Chambers, a lecturer at the University of Cambridge who researched women’s involvement for the register project, said: “This research really shows that this was not just a flash in the pan. Across the entirety of the Royal African Company and its various guises, there were women contributing financially and expecting a financial return from the slave trade.”","[C] Under English law, women who were single or widowed were in control of their own property and could operate as legal persons while married women could not. “That becomes really important for the Royal African Company as it stutters between financial crises,” Chambers said. “Women provided this important well of capital.”","[D] Women invested from the earliest years of enslavement, from Queen Elizabeth I’s backing in the 1560s to Lady Craven’s £1,000 loan financing a voyage to the Gambia through the Guinea Company. Some investors, unable to write their names, signed company records with a spidery “X”.","[E] More than 1,000 women invested in the slave trade, challenging the conventional notion that they were passive beneficiaries and largely fought for its abolition. Researchers found women bought, sold and brokered shares in the Royal African Company (RAC), South Sea Company, and other separate ventures, and used profits from the trafficking of enslaved Africans to secure financial independence and provide for their families. By the time the RAC, which trafficked about 150,000 enslaved people, was dissolved in 1752, women made up about 10% of shareholders.","[F] The research also found that because female investors seemingly did not vote or hold board positions, they often relied on informal efforts to influence and shape a company. Meeting minutes show women acting as witnesses, running the meeting house, delivering the goods exchanged for African lives, petitioning for wages, passing information and, most importantly, lending money and buying and selling shares.","[G] The archives include letters in which women discuss profits from “African stock”, while company records show one investor, Helen Gladman, asking the RAC to transport a young African girl from Sherbrooke Island in Sierra Leone to England to serve in her household. Researchers found women were involved “at almost every level” of the company’s activities. They acted as brokers, supplied goods traded on Africa’s Atlantic coast, managed company property and used their familial and social networks to strengthen the company’s finances and political influence.","[H] In the early 18th century, the RAC secretary, John Perry, wrote to female investors urging them to exchange company debts for shares and persuade friends and relatives to do the same. Chambers said: “That is a financial project, but it is also a political one, because he knows that they might not hold official positions, but women were very influential with their family members and with the way companies were perceived.”","E | 41 | 42 | 43 | B | 44 | 45 | H"],"items":[{"number":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"A","kicker":"【答案】A","analysis":["【定位】固定段E之后；空位42前。","【解析】E段提出 More than 1,000 women invested，并点名 RAC、South Sea Company 等对象；【A】首句的 Register of British Slave Traders 说明证据来源，shows women from across society 把总量发现扩展到阶层广度。它也为后文档案证据和研究者评价铺垫。","逐项分析"]},{"number":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"G","kicker":"【答案】G","analysis":["【定位】空位42；空位43和固定段B前。","【解析】【A】已说明登记册显示女性广泛参与；【G】的 archives include letters 和 company records 把“登记”推进到具体证据，并写明女性担任 broker、供应货物、管理财产和动员社会网络。这些活动也为固定段 B 中 contributing financially and expecting a financial return 提供支撑。","逐项分析"]},{"number":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"D","kicker":"【答案】D","analysis":["【定位】空位43；空位44前。","【解析】固定段 B 强调这种参与不是 flash in the pan，而是贯穿 Royal African Company；【D】首句 Women invested from the earliest years 直接展开时间纵深，并以 Elizabeth I 和 Lady Craven 的实例证明早期投资并非孤例。","逐项分析"]},{"number":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"F","kicker":"【答案】F","analysis":["【定位】空位44；空位45前。","【解析】【D】说明女性从很早开始投资；【F】用 The research also found 补充另一层发现：她们很少投票或担任董事，而靠作见证、运送货物、请愿、借钱和买卖股份施加影响。这种非正式参与自然引出【C】对单身、寡居和已婚女性法律地位的说明。","逐项分析"]},{"number":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"C","kicker":"【答案】C","analysis":["【定位】空位45；固定段H之前。","【解析】【C】解释单身和寡居女性能控制财产、作为法律主体行动，而已婚女性不能，因此她们成为 RAC 财政危机中的 well of capital。固定段 H 中公司秘书敦促女性把债务换成股份并动员亲友，正依赖这种资本与影响力。","逐项分析","干扰项设置","本题主要用证据层和解释层错位。【A】【G】【F】都涉及女性参与，但分别对应“登记册范围”“档案证据”“非正式机制”；若把它们集中在同一段，会掩盖文章从发现到法律解释再到公司策略的推进。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语新题型大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。目前是在测试阶段，该题型仅提供到12月底。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"9.22 精读(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":1474440,"date":"2026-09-22","range":"","title":"Women also helped to fund the","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.22 精读(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.22 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":54594,"date":"2026-09-22","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.22 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.22检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":60368,"date":"2026-09-22","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.22检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.22检验题__新题型__段落排序(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":73920,"date":"2026-09-22","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.22检验题__新题型__段落排序(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"9.22杂志排版(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":761692,"date":"2026-09-22","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.22杂志排版(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
